WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.930
- Your new album,

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:02.990
it's a bit of a throw back
to your early days, right?

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:03.823
- Yeah.

00:00:03.823 --> 00:00:04.870
- Okay. So what does this mean?

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.530
Is this like stuff you wrote
like in your early days?

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.380
- Yeah. That's what happened,
you know, when you're,

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.540
when you're doing your well,
your first, my first three,

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.410
four albums before I had children
and had a life, you know?

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.370
I used to, you know,

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.670
just write all the time
when I was all at home

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:18.503
and on the bus.

00:00:18.503 --> 00:00:21.330
And so I had a bunch
of songs and, you know,

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.240
you only put 10 on an album.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.400
So I had some leftover and a
few years ago, I went back to,

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.740
I was maybe going to do
a box sex didn't happen,

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.560
ended up changing management
and going off my record label

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:32.393
and everything.

00:00:32.393 --> 00:00:35.580
But I had recorded these songs a few years

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.440
ago that I had written 30 years ago.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.620
And it was really exciting
because they were, you know,

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.230
I'm no longer, you know,
I'm the only one, you know,

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.810
I'm no longer broken
hearted thank goodness,

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.600
I'm much healthier and
have a great relationship.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.830
So I'm not writing those songs.

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:53.610
So it was great to go back
to when I was and pull

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.390
those songs out and kinda sing
with that rock feeling again,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.223
pull them up.

00:00:58.223 --> 00:01:00.123
So if you like that older
stuff, this album, and it's the-

00:01:00.123 --> 00:01:01.958
- I think a lot of us liked it

00:01:01.958 --> 00:01:05.680
- You know, you know, its okay
(audience clapping)

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.940
So this album is filled,
filled with songs like that.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.610
And the one I'm going
to play for you today

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.750
is right around the
"I'm the only one" time,

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:13.974
you know, it's like, really, it's rockin'.

00:01:13.974 --> 00:01:14.807
- [Kelly] Oh my god I love that.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:15.660
And there are so many songs

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.320
people don't realize that we all write,

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.790
and then they don't make
it just because whatever,

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:21.750
for whatever reasons,
a lot of it's politics.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:22.880
- Well, yeah, well,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.070
a lot of these songs that are on the album

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:28.920
were very feminist based
and very kind of strong.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.710
And this is 1989, 1990,

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:33.590
and things were really
different back then.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:37.640
And I just sort of said, well,
maybe not this time for that.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.790
And then they faded away.
- [Kelly] Perfect now!

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:43.030
So perfect! It's like
not a problem at all now.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.100
- Agreed. Agreed.
- Yeah.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.440
Was writing different for
you back in those days

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.650
before you came out? Was it harder?

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:49.483
- Harder.

00:01:49.483 --> 00:01:51.600
- Or was it more clever? Did
you have to be more clever

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.433
about it?

00:01:52.433 --> 00:01:55.540
- Exactly it focused
it because I wanted to,

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.610
I wanted to write what was
really going on, you know,

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:00.810
I wanted to write personally
and what was happening,

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.780
but I didn't want to "oh,
she's that lesbian artist."

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:04.820
You know, I'm only singing about women.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:05.860
- [Kelly] You don't want
to be boxed in one thing

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:09.900
- Exactly. So I learned to be
non-gender specific, you know?

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.290
- Which is also very now.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.317
- There you, also very, indeed!

00:02:13.317 --> 00:02:14.817
- You were ahead of the times!

